FINAL ANSWER:
Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson own most of the code. The default blame view is misleading because of the reformat commit.

**Why the default view is wrong:** `62628c0` ("style: reformat js with 4-space indent and double quotes") was committed by "Fiona Formatter". Plain `git blame` credits her with 1016 surviving lines, and the git-historian `blame_summary` shows 89.9% of `lib/index.js` as hers. Those lines were only re-indented and re-quoted. She did not write them.

`.git-blame-ignore-revs` already lists that commit, but `blame.ignoreRevsFile` isn't set in git config, so git doesn't use the file. I re-ran blame with `--ignore-revs-file` and `-w -M -C`. The historian tool doesn't use the file either.

**Surviving lines with the reformat ignored** (all tracked text files):

| Author | Lines |
|---|---|
| Troy Goode | 809 |
| Douglas Christopher Wilson | 625 |
| Íñigo Marquínez Prado | 95 |
| Jon Church | 72 |
| Sebastian Beltran | 67 |
| Ulises Gascón | 52 |
| Ignacio Mangas | 44 |
| Alejandro Caravaca Puchades | 30 |
| Linus Unnebäck | 26 |
| Ollie Buck | 17 |

Troy Goode and Douglas Christopher Wilson together own about 70% of the top-12 lines.

**Source and tests only** (`lib/index.js` and `test/*.js`):
- Troy Goode has 676 lines.
- Douglas Christopher Wilson has 392.
- Everyone else has 30 or fewer. The next three are Alejandro Caravaca Puchades (30), Eric di Domenico (16) and Alberto Leal (15).

`lib/index.js` is mostly Troy Goode's code. Its oldest line is from 2013-01-31. Douglas Christopher Wilson is the second main owner.

Caveats:
- The top-12 table is cut off at 12 authors, so the tail isn't shown.
- Lines moved across files by `-M -C` are credited to whoever first wrote them.
- The percentages in the table are my reading of these counts, not output from a tool.

To make plain `git blame` ignore the reformat commit, run `git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs`. I haven't changed any config.

